page('index.html','A clearer home for your savings.','Compare nationally marketed banks, understand deposit requirements, and leave room for insured interest. All research is ready to read—no inputs required.', '''<div class="cards"><section class="card"><div class="small">Highest confirmed base APY in this shortlist</div><div class="big">3.50%</div><h3>Marcus</h3><p class="small">As of October 21, 2026. Variable rate; not a market-wide winner.</p>'''+links('marcus')+'''</section><section class="card"><div class="small">Standard FDIC coverage</div><div class="big">$250,000</div><h3>Principal + interest</h3><p class="small">Per depositor, per insured bank, per ownership category.</p>'''+links('fdic','fdic-interest')+'''</section><section class="card"><div class="small">Planning opening & funding date</div><div class="big">Oct 22, 2026</div><h3>A dated snapshot</h3><p class="small">Rates checked today; most bank rate dates are October 21. Funding today is an illustration, not an executed transaction.</p><a href="sources.html">Read the evidence ledger →</a></section></div><div class="notice"><strong>Starting recommendation:</strong> Marcus is the strongest confirmed base-rate option among these accounts. Capital One and Amex tie at 3.20%, followed by Ally at 3.10%. This is a curated shortlist, not an exhaustive list of all national banks or every product tier. Synchrony is not ranked because its official page conflicts with itself.</div><h2>Your research, organized</h2><div class="two"><section class="card"><h3>Choose an account</h3><p>Opening deposits, fees, rates, and unresolved items side by side.</p><a href="accounts.html">Compare all 10 entries →</a></section><section class="card"><h3>Protect the full balance</h3><p>See returns on $10k to $250k, plus interest headroom and a multi-bank example.</p><a href="returns.html">Explore returns & coverage →</a></section></div><h2>What “best” means here</h2><p>Highest confirmed, non-promotional APY in the researched set, with no monthly maintenance fee for the ranked accounts. We include major branch-bank alternatives even when their rates cannot be verified. Bank security controls are documented, not independently audited or scored. No bank can be guaranteed fraud-proof.</p><p><a href="review.html">Read all limitations and flagged irregularities →</a></p>''')
