page('accounts.html','Compare the shortlist.','10 researched entries across major branch banks and nationally marketed online banks. Empty numeric cells mean unverified—not zero.', '<label for="search">Find a bank or status</label><br><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search accounts…"><p id="count" class="small" role="status">10 accounts shown</p>'+table(['Bank / product','Base APY','Minimum to open','Monthly maintenance fee / one waiver','Bank rate date','Evidence status','Official source'],rows)+'<p class="small">¹ Capital One comparison/application page confirms 3.20%; effective October 21 in official indexed application text. Other official product/disclosure extractions show NaN. See Flagged for Review. All confirmed savings rates are variable; no fixed investment term. Fees shown are maintenance fees, not exhaustive transaction charges. Entry list is curated, not an official size ranking.</p>')
money=lambda x:f'${x:,.2f}'
ranked=[a for a in A if a[1] is not None]
rows=[]
for name,apy,_,_,_,_,key in ranked:
 for p in [10000,50000,100000,240000,250000]:
  r=apy/100; interest=p*r
  rows.append([e(name.split(' •')[0]),money(p),money(p*((1+r)**(92/365)-1)),money(p*((1+r)**(182/365)-1)),money(interest),money(p+interest),money(max(0,p+interest-250000)),links(key,'fdic-interest')])
headroom=[]
for name,apy,*rest in ranked:
 r=apy/100;p=math.floor(250000/(1+r)*100)/100
 headroom.append([e(name.split(' •')[0]),f'{apy:.2f}%',money(p),money(250000-p),money(p*(1+r)),links(rest[-1],'fdic','fdic-interest')])
page('returns.html','Returns, with room for insurance.','Calculated scenarios, not bank quotations. Assumed opened and fully funded October 22, 2026; no deposits, withdrawals, fees, bonuses or taxes.', '<div class="notice warn"><strong>$250,000 is not a safe set-and-forget opening deposit.</strong> FDIC coverage includes accrued interest. Existing checking, savings and CDs in the same category at the same bank use the same limit. Higher variable rates or bonuses can exceed the modeled headroom.</div><h2>Interest by deposit size</h2><p>92 days: January 22, 2027 · 182 days: April 22, 2027 · 365 days: October 22, 2027. All balances assume today’s APY stays constant. Actual bank crediting, funding delays and rounding can differ.</p>'+table(['Bank','Opening deposit','92-day interest','182-day interest','365-day interest','365-day balance','Above $250k at year end²','Rate & coverage sources'],rows)+ '<h2>One-year deposit ceiling under unchanged rates</h2><p>Derived opening amounts leave space for 365 days of interest and are rounded down to cents. These are model outputs—not bank opening requirements, and not unconditional coverage guarantees. Assumes no other same-category deposits at that bank.</p>'+table(['Bank','APY','Modeled maximum opening deposit','Interest headroom','Modeled year-end balance','Official inputs'],headroom)+'<h2>A simpler buffer strategy</h2><p>Using a $240,000 opening deposit at Marcus produces a modeled $8,400 interest and $248,400 balance after one year, leaving $1,600 of unused coverage if the 3.50% APY holds. For larger savings, split funds among separately insured banks rather than merely opening more accounts or using more branches of the same bank.</p>'+table(['Scenario','Opening allocation','365-day interest','365-day total','Official inputs'],[['$500,000 illustration','Marcus $240,000; Amex $240,000; Ally $20,000',money(8400+7680+620),money(500000+8400+7680+620),links('marcus','amex','ally','fdic')]])+'<p>No claimed global optimal allocation: the example prioritizes simple buffers and uses only three independently named banking institutions; actual ownership and other deposits must be checked. Discover is not a separate diversification bank from Capital One.</p><h2>Formula & rate risk</h2><p><code>Interest = principal × ((1 + APY/100)^(days/365) − 1)</code><br><code>Opening ceiling = floor(250000 / (1 + APY/100) × 100) / 100</code></p><p>For $100,000, a full-year APY of 2.50%, 3.50%, or 4.50% would yield $2,500, $3,500, or $4,500. These are hypothetical sensitivity cases, not forecasts. The savings account has no guaranteed investment lifespan; the 92/182/365-day horizons are planning windows. CDs may lock rates but bring term and withdrawal constraints; no ambiguous CD rate has been attributed to a specific term here.</p><p class="small">² Excess column assumes a single owner, single ownership category, no other deposits at that bank. It is not a personalized FDIC determination. '+links('fdic','fdic-interest','capital-merger')+'</p>')
page('promotions.html','Bonuses without the guesswork.','Promotions are separate from base returns. A referral benefit is not an unconditional cash opening bonus.',table(['Bank / offer','Confirmed benefit','Requirements / duration','Deposit requirement','Cash bonus / expiry','Status / source'],[['Marcus referral','+1.00 percentage-point APY for 3 months','New recipient must use customer’s referral link. Referrer and new customer can qualify; standard rate afterward. Full terms and qualification timing not fully verified.','No minimum for base savings; referral-specific conditions unverified','','Partially verified; excluded from return model.<br>'+links('referral','marcus')],*[[e(a[0]),'','','','','Opening cash bonus and current promotion eligibility unverified; no bonus assumed.<br>'+links(a[-1])] for a in A[1:]]])+'<div class="notice warn">Blank promotion cells do not mean there are no offers. No unconditional current cash savings-opening bonus was confirmed in the reviewed sources. Targeted, bundled checking, expired and third-party offers are not treated as available savings bonuses.</div><h2>Do not annualize a temporary boost</h2><p>A three-month boost does not pay for twelve months. Marcus itself illustrates a combined 3.75% annual APY for one referral under an unchanged standard APY assumption. That illustration is not used in our base table; personal eligibility, timing, and full terms remain flagged. '+links('referral')+'</p>')
