page('review.html','Flagged for Review','Published limitations are visible here; they are not hidden behind a “verified” label. Unverified items do not prevent publication.',table(['Issue','Finding','Treatment','Official review links'],flags))
page('sources.html','The evidence behind every row.','Official bank and government sources only. Checked October 22, 2026 via retrieved official text or official-domain search excerpts. Dates below distinguish bank disclosure dates from our check date.', '<div class="notice">Verification is field-level, not a blanket endorsement. A source link does not make every product term verified. The notes state exactly what was observed. Return rows link to the official rate inputs, but their dollar values are our labeled calculations.</div>'+table(['ID','Official source','Observed evidence / limits','Checked'],[[e(k),links(k),e(v[2]),'2026-10-22'] for k,v in S.items()])+'<h2>Method</h2><p>Reviewed the starting repository line by line: it contained only a one-line README and no financial dataset to preserve. Selected nationally marketed banks with major consumer brands; avoided small local institutions and fintech pass-through accounts. Official retrieval took priority over search snippets. Conflicting or unconfirmed numeric values are empty and flagged. Third-party comparison-bank rates displayed on Marcus are not used as verification of competitors. Bank marketing multiples of the national average are not adopted as independent benchmarks.</p><p>Every table row has official source links. Computed outputs are labeled and use only confirmed base APYs. Full terms, personal eligibility, and real-time underwriting cannot be confirmed by public-page research alone.</p><p><a href="evidence.json">Download evidence ledger (JSON)</a></p>')
(OUT/'evidence.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checked':'2026-10-22','opening_date_scenario':'2026-10-22','sources':{k:{'title':v[0],'url':v[1],'observed':v[2]} for k,v in S.items()},'accounts':[dict(zip(['name','apy_percent','minimum_opening','monthly_fee_notes','rate_date','status','source_id'],a)) for a in A]},indent=2)+'\n')
